theorem a-define-on-an-open-interval
  note        A define's domain is read where a set is wanted, as the right
              of ∈ is: for t ∈ (a, b) runs over the open interval between a
              and b, not the pair of them.
  let a ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let b ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  let h(t) = t + 1, for t ∈ (a, b)                                    (D1)
         reads one more than t
  then h is a function on (a, b)

1.  h is a function on (a, b)
    D1
